From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: pointer routed events, boxed AddHandler delegates, TextBox TextChanging/SelectionChanged

No pointer event was raised, so React Native for Windows, which takes the pointer from its root view's PointerPressed/Moved/Released, never saw a click: OneDrive's Sign in button did nothing. Mouse messages to an island now raise PointerEntered, Moved, Pressed, Released, Exited, WheelChanged and CaptureLost on the element under the pointer (or the one that captured it), bubbling up while not handled. Handlers added with handledEventsToo see them all the way. PointerRoutedEventArgs give the mouse as a Pointer, GetCurrentPoint relative to any element with the buttons held and what changed, and the modifier keys. UIElement.AddHandler unboxes a handler given boxed (C++/WinRT's box_value, an IReference whose Value is the delegate); calling the box itself wrote over the sender. TextBox raises TextChanging (before TextChanged) and SelectionChanged, which React Native's text input reads its text from: OneDrive's Sign in button now enables as an address is typed and starts the sign-in.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
index 09ec3cb..691dd30 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui.xaml/Makefile.in
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ SOURCES = \
