+ * element under the pointer (or the one that captured it) and bubbles up to the root while not
+ * handled; handlers added with handledEventsToo still see it.  Its PointerRoutedEventArgs give the
+ * pointer (the mouse, id 1), the point relative to any element with the buttons held and what
+ * changed (PointerPoint, PointerPointProperties), and the modifier keys.  PointerEntered and
+ * PointerExited follow the element under the pointer.  Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0
+ * (MIT) and Wine's Windows.UI.Input / Windows.Devices.Input IDL.
+ */
+
